<title>UK: Clarke says go cut UK central government costs.</title>
<headline>Clarke says go cut UK central government costs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday the government expected to cut central government running costs by a further seven percent by 2000.</p>
<p>&quot;We have cut overall central government departments' running costs by eight percent in real terms since the start of this parliament and we are going to reduce them by a further seven percent by the end of the decade.</p>
<p>&quot;Civil Service numbers are already below 1/2 million, and we now expect this fall to continue,&quot; Clarke said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 2274</p>
</text>
